    "section_accordions_xDeiqR": {
      "type": "section-accordions",
      "blocks": {
        "text_WEhTVR": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What types of grass seed grow well in Aspen’s high-altitude climate?",
            "text": "<p>Aspen’s elevation and short growing season call for hardy, cool-season grass seed. Blends like the<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/pitkin-county-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> Rivendell Pitkin County Seed Mix</a> and<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/rivendells-native-low-grow-seed-mix?_pos=1&_sid=a165ca018&_ss=r\" target=\"_blank\"> Native Low Grow Mix</a> are developed for mountain conditions and do well in dry, rocky soils. These mixes are made with native grasses and species that hold up to cold nights, low water, and patchy sun. You can explore our full<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/collections/grass-seeds\" target=\"_blank\"> grass seed collection</a> for more options suited to the region.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_czN6Mm": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I choose the right grass seed for my lawn, slope, or pasture?",
            "text": "<p>The best grass seed depends on what kind of space you're planting and how it's used. Here's a simple way to match your project with the right type of seed:</p><ul><li>For home lawns or backyards that get a mix of sun and activity, look for a reliable cool-season blend that provides strong coverage. A<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/mastergreen-bluegrass-blend-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> bluegrass mix</a> is often used for this purpose because it handles foot traffic well and looks clean and full.</li><li>For shady areas like the side of a house, under trees, or near fences, choose seed that tolerates limited sunlight.<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/ark-valley-premium-shade-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> Shade-tolerant mixes</a> or<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/ark-valley-premium-shade-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> fine fescue</a> blends are made for these conditions and can fill in slower-growing spots.</li><li>For slopes or areas prone to erosion, native and low-grow seed mixes are helpful because they hold soil in place and require less upkeep once established. These are often used on hillsides and ditches, like the<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/rivendells-mountain-pasture-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> Mountain Pasture Seed Mix</a> or<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/buffalo-brand-low-grow-reclamation-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> reclamation blends</a>.</li><li>For large pastures or grazing land, pasture-specific mixes are ideal. These are made up of hardy species that grow back after grazing, such as<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/foragemax-pasturemax\" target=\"_blank\"> pasture blends</a> or<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/horsemax-pasturemax-seed\" target=\"_blank\"> equine mixes</a>.</li><li>For quick repairs or overseeding, use a fast-germinating seed to fill bare patches before cooler weather sets in.<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/triple-star-perennial-ryegrass-blend\" target=\"_blank\"> Perennial ryegrass blends</a> are commonly used for this since they sprout quickly and work well for short-term fixes.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "text_BA96Pr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do you carry native grasses or wildflower seed mixes for this region?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, we stock quality native grass and wildflower seed blends that are adapted to the local climate. These are ideal for open space projects, low-maintenance lawns, or cover crops. Our<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/rivendells-native-low-grow-seed-mix?variant=41994609950909\" target=\"_blank\"> Native Low Grow Mix</a> includes grasses suited to Western Colorado, and we also carry wildflower seed mixes for adding color and pollinator value.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_rtUkF7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are the most popular grass seed blends for homes in Aspen?",
            "text": "<p>For residential lawns, people often choose<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/mastergreen-sun-shade-carefree-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> MasterGreen Sun & Shade Carefree</a>,<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/triple-star-perennial-ryegrass-blend\" target=\"_blank\"> Triple Star Ryegrass Blend</a>, or<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/chantilly-creeping-red-fescue-seed\" target=\"_blank\"> Chantilly Creeping Red Fescue</a>. These mixes are great for uneven light, patchy spots, and general lawn repair. Their performance holds up well through the seasons, and they’re flexible enough to use for overseeding or starting from scratch.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_QcDyz7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use turf grass seed for golf courses, sports areas, or high-traffic lawns?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, we have turf grass blends designed for active areas. For example, the<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/ark-valley-sports-turf-grass-seed-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> Ark Valley Vitaly Sports Turf Mix</a> and<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/products/ph-d-world-cup-f3000-perennial-rye-mix\" target=\"_blank\"> Ph.D World Cup Perennial Rye Mix</a> are commonly used for sports fields and golf course edges. These grasses offer durability and quick recovery, making them ideal for high-foot-traffic spaces.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_PgeKF8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When is the best time to plant grass seed in Aspen — spring or fall?",
            "text": "<p>Cool-season grasses do best when planted in early fall, once the summer heat has passed and the soil is still warm. Spring is also possible, but cold nights and late snow can slow germination. To get the timing right and avoid reseeding, check your location's weather and follow this<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/blogs/news/when-to-plant-bulk-grass-seed-for-best-results\" target=\"_blank\"> seasonal planting guide</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_Fd8c9W": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much grass seed do I need to cover my yard or project site?",
            "text": "<p>It depends on the seed variety, seeding rate, and how thick you want your coverage. A 50 lb bag of bluegrass seed can cover up to 10,000 square feet, which is a good quantity for most residential lawns. Native grasses or pasture seed may need more per acre depending on species and ground condition. The seeding rate matters when you’re planning a larger area or working with uneven terrain. Using the right amount from the start helps promote strong, even growth and saves time in the long run.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_fefCcQ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What should I do to prepare my soil before spreading seed?",
            "text": "<p>Good soil prep is one of the most important factors for seed success. Start by clearing debris, loosening the soil, and mixing in compost or fertilizer to improve germination. Adding a thin layer of topsoil can also help new grass root faster.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_hCzz3i": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I just throw seed on the dirt, or do I need to overseed and mulch?",
            "text": "<p>Grass seed needs good seed-to-soil contact to sprout. Tossing it on bare dirt rarely works as well as raking it in lightly and covering with straw or mulch. This helps retain moisture and protects the seed from wind or runoff.<a href=\"https://www.rivendelldistribution.com/blogs/news/what-to-know-before-buying-bagged-compost\" target=\"_blank\"> Using the right compost</a> or erosion-control material makes a noticeable difference during germination.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_cfe7R3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do you offer advice or help selecting seed mixes for specific areas or conditions?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, our team is made up of knowledgeable staff who know what works in this region’s climate, soil types, and growing seasons. At Rivendell Distribution, we take pride in offering friendly, local service to help you choose the right seed for your lawn, pasture, hillside, or shaded area.</p><p>If you're working on a large project or looking for a deal on bulk seed, we can help you make the most of your budget. Shop our full selection online or visit us at<a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Rivendell+Distribution,+Inc./@39.4839284,-107.228341,17z/data=!4m6!3m5!1s0x8741a857da136551:0xe31190bbf15ca07c!8m2!3d39.4839284!4d-107.228341!16s%2Fg%2F1tdh4bgk?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDYwMi4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\" target=\"_blank\"> 3961 Co Rd 114, Glenwood Springs, CO</a>.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
